cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Lattice: a crypto-agility and post-quantum-readiness scanner"
message: "If you use Lattice in research or tooling, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Lattice contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/mk12002/Lattice"
url: "https://github.com/mk12002/Lattice"
abstract: >-
  Lattice statically analyzes a codebase, produces a CycloneDX-style
  Cryptographic Bill of Materials (CBOM), grades every cryptographic usage for
  quantum vulnerability (Shor/Grover) and classical weakness, and emits a
  prioritized migration roadmap toward the NIST post-quantum standards
  (FIPS 203/204/205). It covers 12 languages plus configuration and dependency
  manifests, has zero runtime dependencies, and is deterministic and offline.
keywords:
  - cryptography
  - post-quantum
  - cbom
  - crypto-agility
  - static-analysis
  - sbom
  - security
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.4.0
